        {
          "id": "SP_LEPTASTREA_TRANSVERSA_KLUNZINGER_1879",
          "name": "Leptastrea transversa Klunzinger, 1879",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "crust coral",
          "lineage": "Leptastrea",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Notes for local identification: Colonies are encrusting to sub-massive, light brown or creamy with creamy brown tentacles. The polyps sometimes have grayish-green mouth parts. Corallites are bigger than in L. pruinosa (some corallites with more than 5 mm width). Septa plunge steeply, which leave a wide columellae and deeper corallites in comparison to L. pruinosa. Abundance: uncommon. Depth of occurrence: About 3 m.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
